{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant","id":390220,"title":"Is the sphere of Entropy redundant?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-02T12:53:22-08:00","id":390220,"title":"Is the sphere of Entropy redundant?","content":"As the topic says, is the sphere of entropy actually needed in the game? Does it just step on the toes of other spheres?<br /> <br /> Specifically what can Entropy do is not replicated by other spheres?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":".  clarity 02-02-2015, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T13:06:58-08:00","id":390241,"title":"","content":"Why do you think it might be redundant? I can think of a bunch of uses that other Spheres would struggle to replicate with ease. It's a feature of the Sphere system that there are many ways to skin a cat - some Spheres are better suited to certain cats than others. Look at its uses for manipulating long-term chance and destiny, for example. It's clearly the best choice for those kinds of Effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T13:21:19-08:00","id":390260,"title":"","content":"No, I do not think it redundant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T13:36:28-08:00","id":390300,"title":"","content":"Redundant? well it's true that many of it's effects can be duplicated with a little bit of imagination but you will always need several spheres to pull it off. In fact the same can be said by many other spheres, you can do what others can with the right idea and combination. Entropy affects something that no other sphere can, your dice. It can be a little bit meta but entropy gives you precision, it increases the probability of success. No other sphere does that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 02-02-2015, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T14:10:52-08:00","id":390322,"title":"","content":"Maybe Entropy 5 mental alteration could be redundant if we think it as Mind with Entropy. Otherwise, no I don't think that it's redundant. For instance: &quot;Luck&quot; can't directly be affected with other spheres, even if its outcome may be replicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T14:25:40-08:00","id":390356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=390300#post390300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Redundant? well it's true that many of it's effects can be duplicated with a little bit of imagination but you will always need several spheres to pull it off. In fact the same can be said by many other spheres, you can do what others king with the right idea and combination. Entropy affects something that no other sphere can, your dice. It can be a little bit meta but entropy gives you precision, it increases the probability of success. No other sphere does that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically what Entropy effects are not replicatable by other Spheres? <br /> <br /> Does it? Isn't affecting the roll of dice simply a forces 2 effect?<br /> <br /> Isn't seeing what is probable just a Time 2 effect?<br /> <br /> Isn't sensing decay just a Life 1 or Matter 1 effect? <br /> <br /> Isn't causing decay just a Life 3 or Matter 3 effect?<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to be a dick just thinking hard about this, that's all. Philosophically the sphere is cool. Mechanically in the game I'm wondering if it isn't needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T14:27:41-08:00","id":390361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=390241#post390241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think it might be redundant? I can think of a bunch of uses that other Spheres would struggle to replicate with ease. It's a feature of the Sphere system that there are many ways to skin a cat - some Spheres are better suited to certain cats than others. Look at its uses for manipulating long-term chance and destiny, for example. It's clearly the best choice for those kinds of Effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mind giving some examples of What does it do that other spheres struggle to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T14:33:41-08:00","id":390389,"title":"","content":"to an extend many sphere effects can be replicated by compining many more.<br /> <br /> for instance in an older forums i saw a rote(life 3 forces 3 prime 2 mind 1) that replicated time 3 in giving many actions per turn<br /> <br /> hermes brand is replicated(though not identicallly i think) in dark ages mage with primus 3 vires 3 anima 3. i know pillars are different but.. honestly.. i think this particular effect could propably work like that in modern mage too. prime life and forces. basically vampires eating your blood burn..<br /> <br /> spirit 4 in dead magic can get you and others in the shadowlands just like life 4 spirit 3(4 for many people) entropy 4.(from void engineers revised. though perhaps their paradigm makes this necessary.)<br /> <br /> forces 3 life 3 inconvention book progenitors is, IIRC also achievable by life 4.<br /> <br /> there are propably more examples like this too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T14:39:43-08:00","id":390400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=390389#post390389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">to an extend many sphere effects can be replicated by compining many more.<br /> <br /> for instance in an older forums i saw a rote(life 3 forces 3 prime 2 mind 1) that replicated time 3 in giving many actions per turn<br /> <br /> hermes brand is replicated(though not identicallly i think) in dark ages mage with primus 3 vires 3 anima 3. i know pillars are different but.. honestly.. i think this particular effect could propably work like that in modern mage too. prime life and forces. basically vampires eating your blood burn..<br /> <br /> spirit 4 in dead magic can get you and others in the shadowlands just like life 4 spirit 3(4 for many people) entropy 4.(from void engineers revised. though perhaps their paradigm makes this necessary.)<br /> <br /> forces 3 life 3 inconvention book progenitors is, IIRC also achievable by life 4.<br /> <br /> there are propably more examples like this too</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not picking on the other spheres for a reason - while one can definitely skin a cat in more ways than one, no other sphere seems so replaceable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T15:00:17-08:00","id":390414,"title":"","content":"I really don't have a good answer since entropy has never been my strength but for me it represents the concepts of destiny, fate and luck. For me they are different enough to the other spheres to have it's own sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T15:27:59-08:00","id":390459,"title":"","content":"Time 2 you can take a look at the specfic future of your immediate environment for a set time jump forwards. Mixed with the other spheres it can show you or focus on things, people, places etc. It cannot show you the threads of causality, fate and other effects that cause the events to be thus. It cannot show you How altering any piece of the Present may effect the Future you're seeing. With Entropy this is possible, likewise for looking backwards at causes leading to the present events and the possible divergences. <br /> <br /> No other Sphere lets you manipulate these threads of fate or causality either with any certain knowledge of what you're achieving. Not to mention completely breaking Causality without eradicating portions of Time itself. The other Spheres might be able to simulate an act of Luck in limited aspects but Luck itself is Entropy's domain and that's really important because not everything that's &quot;lucky&quot; can be duplicated by other spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T15:44:48-08:00","id":390522,"title":"","content":"There are a great many things that are covered by multiple spheres... and if we focus on the desired result instead of the process, that number grows to infinity.<br /> <br /> Regarding Entropy 5 being replaced by Mind... maybe with a butt-load of successes. Mind can create thoughts and remove thoughts, but can it affect the probability of a thought NEVER or ALWAYS occurring? It needs at least Time to do that, and even still... you would have to forcibly change every possibility, which with time goes to infinity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Entropy and Prime both cross a lot of borders. Entropy often combines with other spheres to provide them precision in targeting, choosing, or blending.<br /> <br /> Take for example an engine. You could Matter/Time it with some awesome power, but it would still break down. Everything breaks down. So to keep that engine running at a supernatural level you need either continuous Matter/Time maintenance to keep each component in tip top condition, or to make it self-replicating and feed it Quintessence. With Entropy though, you can remove the inherent imperfections in the system (which is all the little components AND how they interact) resulting in a system that does -not- break down over time.<br /> <br /> Entropy in common language is a word used to signify disorder, but scientifically it is a unit used to measure the amount of disorder. All systems (patterns for our discussion) have SOME level of disorder to them (low levels generally called order)... Entropy changes that.<br /> <br /> It can also radiate the same. At higher levels you can attach an &quot;entropy&quot; aura to living creatures, and even minds. That means you can apply curses, blessings, and such. Add some Prime and you can make these permanent.<br /> <br /> Entropy deals with a <i>quality</i> of the patterns that other spheres create. It deals with <i>versions</i> of primal energies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":2211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","user":"SixFootChicken","date":". 02-02-2015, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T17:29:30-08:00","id":390695,"title":"","content":"You know whut would be useful? A primer on the more esoteric Spheres. This is due to the fact that two of my Mage Players are new and they posses Enthropy and Prime.<br /> They're having trouble getting beyond, &quot;It makes me Lucky&quot; and &quot;I use it to create Talismans.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T19:11:33-08:00","id":390840,"title":"","content":"Oh lord. Did you at least try and sit down with the folks and go through the basics of the Spheres and their levels? Spheres are horrible to new players unless someone can take them by the hand and exactly explain what they are about.<br /> <br /> It's not annuled by saying &quot;a lot of what it does can be done by other spheres&quot; as the same argument applies to every other sphere. Magic is a tool to solve problems. When you have a hammer you use a hammer. That's the approach that can be taken with the spheres quite easily.<br /> <br /> Entropy is chance/luck, fate and decay. In practice this means that this sphere is usually more roundabout in its applications. For instance, while you'd use forces to zap someone dead, you'd use entropy to have a support beam crack and fall on top of his head. When it comes to Fate you use Entropy to see the fate of people or objects and to twist and turn what they may or may not do. For instance you can use Fate on a person to ensure that circumstances conspire that he is at the right place at the right time. You can use Fate to get a gut feeling which is the right choice at a given moment. In essence you use Fate to ensure an outcome or judge the most likely outcome for a given situation. Chance/luck is similar and can be interpreted as an application of Fate. It's all about rigging things so they work in your favour or the favour of people you like - the dice are always double 6s, you always have a winning hand in poker, you hit more often then others, your bullets amazingly ricochet to hit someone in the most improbable manner. Or you inflict the same on others, be it for them to have rotten luck or putting a curse upon their house, where their crops will wilt and their loins will wither, for they angered someone they truly shouldn't have. The final application of Entropy is the literal meaning of the word. Entropy is about decay, studying the process of decay and stopping decay. This means that you can find stress points, push them, have things fall apart, kill people with massive organ failure, decay things into husks, corrode materials and so on.<br /> <br /> Prime on the other hand requires that you actually understand the underlying metaphysics of Magic. That everything in reality is made of primal energies and primal energies are usually quantified as points of Quintessence. Quintessence can be stored within a mage, within an item, within a magical creature or within a whole place. This energy can be harnessed by Mages to improve their powers and efficiency of their spellcasting, as well as to build magical items of their own, this energy is also what makes magical entities tick. Now what does this mean in practice. For one, Prime is the sphere that equalises the playing field for mages with low avatar ratings. It allows them to use more quintessence then their avatar would allow them. For the other it allows them to use any and all forms of quintessence around them as power source - be it blood within their veins, the goat next to them, the Tass they harvested in a forlorn castle or the energy of a deep, calm forest. Prime allows you to manipulate with such core concepts as Paradox and Resonance as well, broadening the esoteric applications of the sphere. It also allows you to counter all magic and dispel all ongoing effects, as well as block and interact with supernatural creatures and their sources of power. It allows you to enchant weapons to do horrendous harm, and it allows you to take ambient quintessence of anything around you and turn it into something else. You know that classic mainstay, the fireball? Prime 2 in that spell is all about allowing you to create &quot;something out of nothing&quot; - you're actually using prime to transmute ambient quintessence into energy for the spell, then forces to turn this energy into fire and toss it at what you want it to blow up. And that's before getting into the fact that Prime also allows you to build magical items and nodes (the afforementioned sources of Quintessence).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T19:54:44-08:00","id":390874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=390695#post390695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know whut would be useful? A primer on the more esoteric Spheres. This is due to the fact that two of my Mage Players are new and they posses Enthropy and Prime.<br /> They're having trouble getting beyond, &quot;It makes me Lucky&quot; and &quot;I use it to create Talismans.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you dare to post their Spheres and Paradigm... we could help specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T20:06:06-08:00","id":390904,"title":"","content":"There should only be 4 spheres really, Life/Mind/Matter/Forces/Entropy, Spirit, Prime, Time/Correspondence. The first 5 are all just forces as matter is energy slowed down, life is just the correct combination of matter and mind is just a part of the body and therefore life. Correspondence is essentially the sphere of space, space and time are actually the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T20:11:54-08:00","id":390908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=390904#post390904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should only be 4 spheres really, Life/Mind/Matter/Forces/Entropy, Spirit, Prime, Time/Correspondence. The first 5 are all just forces as matter is energy slowed down, life is just the correct combination of matter and mind is just a part of the body and therefore life. Correspondence is essentially the sphere of space, space and time are actually the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So says the Technocracy. <br /> <br /> <br /> I see your reality, and substitute my own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T22:08:47-08:00","id":391037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=390874#post390874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you dare to post their Spheres and Paradigm... we could help specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enthanos Samurai type and a 13 year old Hermes. (Mostly sticks to using Prime and Forces to toss around Lightningbolts and Fireballs. So far, she has not yet exploded)<br /> <br /> I sat down with them and spent quite awhile talking about the spheres as best I could but it just all seemed to stumble outta their heads by the next time we met up. Which, given they got other things to worry about, is not surprising. The other three players are two Mage vets that recently joined and a friend that is new to Ascension but Has lots of experience with Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T23:22:19-08:00","id":391087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=390908#post390908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So says the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> <br /> I see your reality, and substitute my own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure he was intentionally doing a <i>reducto ad absurdum</i>.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T23:38:10-08:00","id":391101,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of people focus on the &quot;decay&quot; aspect of Entropy, when the fate/fortune order/chaos stuff is more interesting and has less in common with other Spheres. Here's an example of something you can do relatively easily that would be difficult with other Spheres alone: instant room (or lab, or Hermetic Library, or crime scene)-cleaning. Entropy 3, maybe Matter 2 or Prime 2 Forces 3 as well to cut down a little on the number of required successes--but take away the Entropy and you're looking at a very high number of required successes.<br /> <br /> Anything with Entropy 2 is going to be very hard to replicate with other Spheres. Any phenomenon that can be simply described in terms of probability is very straightforward to affect with Entropy 2. The best thing is is, Entropy is frequently Coincidental (the Etherite lab-organizing grenade being a notable exception).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 02-03-2015, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T05:11:54-08:00","id":391286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=390361#post390361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mind giving some examples of What does it do that other spheres struggle to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think others have covered this well, but my answer would include the following:<br /> <br /> - distinguish chance from purpose, order from disorder<br /> - identify the influence of destiny in the here and now<br /> - control destiny through bloodlines over the course of several generations<br /> - affect the outcome of events without interacting with any Patterns (useful to bypass Pattern-based Wards and Bans)<br /> - create memetic concepts that flourish independently of the caster (Mind cannot do this)<br /> <br /> Those are just a few off the top of my head. You might be able to reproduce similar Effects with other Spheres, but you'd face a hefty success requirement. What Entropy could do with one or two successes might require many more when using another Sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T05:14:37-08:00","id":391291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkuwa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=390904#post390904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should only be 4 spheres really, Life/Mind/Matter/Forces/Entropy, Spirit, Prime, Time/Correspondence. The first 5 are all just forces as matter is energy slowed down, life is just the correct combination of matter and mind is just a part of the body and therefore life. Correspondence is essentially the sphere of space, space and time are actually the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nah it should be one sphere Stuff. Sense stuff. Manipulate Minor stuff. Create minor stuff. Manipulate complex stuff Create complex stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T05:57:35-08:00","id":391329,"title":"","content":"XDXD. That Sphere should be called Magick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Do you mind giving some examples of What does it do that other spheres struggle to do?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>A simple effect that can be done with Entropy and can't be replicated with other spheres? &quot;Bad luck&quot;. You can use Entropy to determine that something &quot;bad&quot; will happen to someone without specifying or even knowing what will be.<br /> Only Entropy allows for such indeterminate and broad manipulations, to affect the outcome in ways your mage don't even knows, but still controlling, in a broad sense, the nature of the outcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-03-2015, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T06:09:45-08:00","id":391333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=391037#post391037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Enthanos Samurai type and a 13 year old Hermes. (Mostly sticks to using Prime and Forces to toss around Lightningbolts and Fireballs. So far, she has not yet exploded)<br /> <br /> I sat down with them and spent quite awhile talking about the spheres as best I could but it just all seemed to stumble outta their heads by the next time we met up. Which, given they got other things to worry about, is not surprising. The other three players are two Mage vets that recently joined and a friend that is new to Ascension but Has lots of experience with Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Without Sphere levels this will be somewhat vague.<br /> <br /> Euthanatos &quot;Samurai&quot; - Assuming he has Entropy, he should use it to focus on making his &quot;Samurai&quot; skills better. His sword strikes should be more accurate and bite more deeply. He should have uncanny good luck, while his opponents trip over themselves. The environment itself should lend him a hand (see the movie Final Destination). He should be a Super-Samurai. He has no weak spots and can always find them on others, especially if combined with any other sphere.<br /> <br /> &quot;Harry Potter&quot; - sorry, lol - Ok so he's good with the direct Forces. Stick with forces and branch out... he can fly, go invisible, create illusions, surge machines, create force fields, SO MUCH STUFF. If I were a Forces/Prime OoH mage, I would pick up Correspondence ASAP - then he can create wards (explosions, alarms, barriers), perform all his magick at range, and eventually teleport or create his own pocket realms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: A samurai should know how to use a bow. With some Entropy and a well placed bow shot, he could create mundane chain reactions. Add a dot of corr or forces to it, or work with his hermetic friend, and the shot itself could be virtually impossible to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":2211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","user":"SixFootChicken","date":". 02-03-2015, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T07:33:29-08:00","id":391416,"title":"","content":"Yesterday, so many brain farts.<br /> Ethanos is as of no Enthropy 3, Correspondence 2 and Mind 2<br /> Hermes is a simple Prime 3 Forces 3 Lucky Fireball Lobber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/1n0ov7p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3881-mental-mouse","name":"Mental-Mouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3881_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T07:55:22-08:00","id":391431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-Mouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=391416#post391416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yesterday, so many brain farts.<br /> Ethanos is as of no Enthropy 3, Correspondence 2 and Mind 2<br /> Hermes is a simple Prime 3 Forces 3 Lucky Fireball Lobber.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>Real quick like, here is a rote database that has been around a long time. Some of the rotes there are garbage, but a lot of them are great inspiration (if not useable directly). <a href=\"http://rotes.theflamingqiviuts.com/findrotes.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rotes.theflamingqiviuts.com/findrotes.php</a></i><br /> <br /> There is so much potential here.<br /> <br /> Entropy 3 lets you sense and control probability (Fate), and alter any predictable pattern. Corr 2 and Mind 2 will take your perception and basically blow it up, expanding it through space and the minds of others.<br /> <br /> Mind 2, Entropy 1, Corr 1<br /> You could automatically win initiative, always, by reading surface thoughts and discerning the most probable attack.<br /> <br /> Entropy 3, Corr 2<br /> As I mentioned earlier, this will allow you to make some small insignificant change nearby, which will result in something big happening somewhere else. Imagine being able to elbow a loose pipe in an alleyway and cause a store-front sign to fall on a passing car.<br /> <br /> Mind 1 Entropy 1 Corr 1 (Corr 2, Entropy 2 for CRAZY trick shots)<br /> Perfect Shot. You would be able to always place a target on the exact weakest point, without spending a lot of time focusing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Entropy 3/Mind 2/Corr 2 should make this guy a legit super-soldier. He can read minds, see around corners (or through walls), and control the fate of anything predictable. All surveilance cameras could fail in his presence with a little Corr 1 Entropy 3 effect. He could use Mind 1 Corr 2 to expand his &quot;mind's eye&quot; to the entire area, and Entropy 3 to plot a safe course through an otherwise deadly firefight. He should specialize in subtlety.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Prime 3 Forces 3<br /> Good lord son, you've got power coming out of your ears.<br /> <br /> Scrolls, potions, and other single use charms should be his strength.<br /> <br /> All the stuff I mentioned before he can easily accomplish... elemental power, flying, invisibility, illusions, force fields, telekenisis, the list goes on and on.<br /> <br /> With Prime 3 though, he can use normal everyday Quintessence (does not need Tass with correct resonance) to make temporary magick items. That means, while yes he can launch a fireball... he can also create invisibility potions, or a scroll that casts a fireball and is destroyed in the process.<br /> <br /> Given enough Tass with appropriate resonance (potential ST carrot), he could even use Prime 3 to make permanent magick items! A wand of Fireballs, or a flying broomstick, or whatever.<br /> <br /> Outside of that (sorry that's a favorite of mine, Prime 3) - He can do creative things like Forces 3 / Prime 3 Anti-Magic Force Field. Any spells cast could be unraveled and used to fuel his own force field.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Forces 3 Prime 3 is very direct and very simplistic. The combinations and versatility it provides are where the complexity lies. He can specialize in subtlety, but I think his strength should be more in versatility.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: The Hermetic creating little &quot;explosion potions&quot; (or arrows) and giving them to the Euthanatos (who can land them perfectly) would probably be a coincidental way to deliver some Forces 3 goodness to your enemies at the worst possible time and place for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":2211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","user":"SixFootChicken","date":". 02-03-2015, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T09:48:32-08:00","id":391565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=390459#post390459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time 2 you can take a look at the specfic future of your immediate environment for a set time jump forwards. Mixed with the other spheres it can show you or focus on things, people, places etc. It cannot show you the threads of causality, fate and other effects that cause the events to be thus. It cannot show you How altering any piece of the Present may effect the Future you're seeing. With Entropy this is possible, likewise for looking backwards at causes leading to the present events and the possible divergences.<br /> <br /> No other Sphere lets you manipulate these threads of fate or causality either with any certain knowledge of what you're achieving. Not to mention completely breaking Causality without eradicating portions of Time itself. The other Spheres might be able to simulate an act of Luck in limited aspects but Luck itself is Entropy's domain and that's really important because not everything that's &quot;lucky&quot; can be duplicated by other spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Time 2 and another sphere at level 1 should be able to show what is going to affect what and how. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=391329#post391329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">XDXD. That Sphere should be called Magick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A simple effect that can be done with Entropy and can't be replicated with other spheres? &quot;Bad luck&quot;. You can use Entropy to determine that something &quot;bad&quot; will happen to someone without specifying or even knowing what will be.<br /> Only Entropy allows for such indeterminate and broad manipulations, to affect the outcome in ways your mage don't even knows, but still controlling, in a broad sense, the nature of the outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so as currently written, I would agree that the spheres have difficulty being &quot;random&quot; and performing &quot;unknowable&quot; effects on a person. <br /> <br /> Bad &quot;luck&quot; could just be partially replicated by adding more successes to a Forces 3, Prime 2, or a Matter 3 ritual to randomly create a force that at some point will cause something specific to the person, break their engine in their car. Maybe Time 4 to delay it. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=390522#post390522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a great many things that are covered by multiple spheres... and if we focus on the desired result instead of the process, that number grows to infinity.<br /> <br /> Regarding Entropy 5 being replaced by Mind... maybe with a butt-load of successes. Mind can create thoughts and remove thoughts, but can it affect the probability of a thought NEVER or ALWAYS occurring? It needs at least Time to do that, and even still... you would have to forcibly change every possibility, which with time goes to infinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should Entropy 5 do a Mind effect 5 with less successes? From a game mechanic point of view,iIf that is the case, why do we have the Sphere of Mind at all? Who says an extra success or two can't make thoughts randomly pop up in a person's head from a Mind effect?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=390522#post390522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take for example an engine. You could Matter/Time it with some awesome power, but it would still break down. Everything breaks down. So to keep that engine running at a supernatural level you need either continuous Matter/Time maintenance to keep each component in tip top condition, or to make it self-replicating and feed it Quintessence. With Entropy though, you can remove the inherent imperfections in the system (which is all the little components AND how they interact) resulting in a system that does -not- break down over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>But in the description of the Sphere itself, (using <a href=\"http://www.snowsidhe.com/ResourceGuide/Mage-Spheres.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.snowsidhe.com/ResourceGuide/Mage-Spheres.htm</a> ) Entropy says it cannot stave off the inevitable. The reason engines break down is because of design imperfections. Everything engineered only has so much accuracy. What is modeled with probability on a computer is not in fact actually, random, it is determined by the forces acting on it and the quality of the materials. Arguably a Matter 3 Forces 2 effect could keep an engine going forever. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=390522#post390522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can also radiate the same. At higher levels you can attach an &quot;entropy&quot; aura to living creatures, and even minds. That means you can apply curses, blessings, and such. Add some Prime and you can make these permanent.<br /> <br /> Entropy deals with a <i>quality</i> of the patterns that other spheres create. It deals with <i>versions</i> of primal energies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But bless a lineage how? Basically what it's doing in is a Life 4, Mind 4, Forces 2 effect: LIfe 4, guarantee good health. Mind 4: Forces them to make good decisions. Also mind control the people who interact with this lineage to give them favourable treatment. Forces 2 to make accidents less likely. Actually when I think about it, a &quot;Blessing&quot; is really kind of a very morally grey area. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=391286#post391286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think others have covered this well, but my answer would include the following:<br /> <br /> 1- distinguish chance from purpose, order from disorder<br /> 2- identify the influence of destiny in the here and now<br /> 3- control destiny through bloodlines over the course of several generations<br /> 4- affect the outcome of events without interacting with any Patterns (useful to bypass Pattern-based Wards and Bans)<br /> 5- create memetic concepts that flourish independently of the caster (Mind cannot do this)<br /> <br /> Those are just a few off the top of my head. You might be able to reproduce similar Effects with other Spheres, but you'd face a hefty success requirement. What Entropy could do with one or two successes might require many more when using another Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I added numbers to this so I can respond to them.<br /> <br /> 1.) But what is chance from purpose? Was someone a dick to me on purpose, or by accident? Mind 3 telepathy. Order from disorder? Shouldn't that be visible to the naked eye? Or even a combination of level 1 Spheres?<br /> <br /> 2.) Depends on how one wants &quot;Fate&quot; or &quot;Destiny&quot; as an independent force in your game. If you don't, (like me) then this isn't even a thing.<br /> <br /> 3.) See above.<br /> <br /> 4.) But arguably this outcomes come from a deterministic process using other spheres. <br /> <br /> 5.) Why not? And if, by description of the Sphere, what is lost by getting rid of Entropy and folding that capability into the Sphere of Mind? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T10:10:27-08:00","id":391596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=391565#post391565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. Time 2 and another sphere at level 1 should be able to show what is going to affect what and how.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, so as currently written, I would agree that the spheres have difficulty being &quot;random&quot; and performing &quot;unknowable&quot; effects on a person.<br /> <br /> Bad &quot;luck&quot; could just be partially replicated by adding more successes to a Forces 3, Prime 2, or a Matter 3 ritual to randomly create a force that at some point will cause something specific to the person, break their engine in their car. Maybe Time 4 to delay it.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Why should Entropy 5 do a Mind effect 5 with less successes? From a game mechanic point of view,iIf that is the case, why do we have the Sphere of Mind at all? Who says an extra success or two can't make thoughts randomly pop up in a person's head from a Mind effect?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> But in the description of the Sphere itself, (using <a href=\"http://www.snowsidhe.com/ResourceGuide/Mage-Spheres.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.snowsidhe.com/ResourceGuide/Mage-Spheres.htm</a> ) Entropy says it cannot stave off the inevitable. The reason engines break down is because of design imperfections. Everything engineered only has so much accuracy. What is modeled with probability on a computer is not in fact actually, random, it is determined by the forces acting on it and the quality of the materials. Arguably a Matter 3 Forces 2 effect could keep an engine going forever.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> But bless a lineage how? Basically what it's doing in is a Life 4, Mind 4, Forces 2 effect: LIfe 4, guarantee good health. Mind 4: Forces them to make good decisions. Also mind control the people who interact with this lineage to give them favourable treatment. Forces 2 to make accidents less likely. Actually when I think about it, a &quot;Blessing&quot; is really kind of a very morally grey area.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I added numbers to this so I can respond to them.<br /> <br /> 1.) But what is chance from purpose? Was someone a dick to me on purpose, or by accident? Mind 3 telepathy. Order from disorder? Shouldn't that be visible to the naked eye? Or even a combination of level 1 Spheres?<br /> <br /> 2.) Depends on how one wants &quot;Fate&quot; or &quot;Destiny&quot; as an independent force in your game. If you don't, (like me) then this isn't even a thing.<br /> <br /> 3.) See above.<br /> <br /> 4.) But arguably this outcomes come from a deterministic process using other spheres.<br /> <br /> 5.) Why not? And if, by description of the Sphere, what is lost by getting rid of Entropy and folding that capability into the Sphere of Mind?<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> By this logic, I challenge you to come up with <i>a single effect</i> that can not be duplicated by another Sphere. Even rank 1 stuff can be jerry-rigged. If you can not do this, then all Spheres are redundant and should be ignored in favor of simplicity. If you can do this once, or even twice... then congratulations you have 2, or possibly 3 spheres.<br /> <br /> <br /> You say Life 4, Mind 4, Forces 2 can &quot;bless&quot; a target. Can it ensure that is passed down genetically? Sure it can, with how many successes?<br /> <br /> Yeah you could use Forces 3, Prime 2, Matter 3, Time 4 to provide a hanging forces effect to overload a car engine... or you could just use Entropy 3. (HUGE difference in power levels there...)<br /> <br /> There is absolutely no sphere that is &quot;required&quot; if your argument is that it can be replicated somehow.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind and Entropy 5 are different things. Mind governs a shit ton of stuff, Entropy 5 is just the rank of Entropy required to affect the chaos inherent in thoughts. You can make thoughts viral, or die out naturally. Entropy 5 does NOT replicate the Mind sphere, no more than Entropy 4 replicates Life or Entropy 3 replicates Matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> You say that everything is perfectly deterministic, so is there one possible future then? If I were in your game world, and I used Mind 3/Time 3 to look into a persons memories, could I instantly determine which memory was MOST important to him? If I were to use Mind 3 / Time 3 to look into his future, could I determine exactly what needs to have him behave the way I want? If I were to use Matter 1 to scan a car, how many successes would I need to find the weakest point?<br /> <br /> <br /> The Spheres are not designed mechanically OOC to be a perfect delineation of the universe. They are designed IC to be representations of fundamental forces of the universe - which are all tangled up together, acting and interacting. By definition there MUST be some overlap. In this context, Entropy governs the fundamental force of &quot;Order&quot;. Yes, by some means of having every other sphere to near master level and amassing massive power through every cast (major successes) you could replicate almost all Entropy effects (based on the ST, of course). The mage who studies order, chaos, and the fundamental force of entropy will have a much easier time of it.<br /> <br /> I could use Correspondence to &quot;summon&quot; any force and control it through shape and relation, with enough successes. A Forces mage would have a much easier time of it.<br /> <br /> I could use Life to fuck with people's Mind, if I knew enough about the relationship between them. A Mind mage can be much more direct about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's how this game works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T10:25:35-08:00","id":391614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SixFootChicken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=391596#post391596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> By this logic, I challenge you to come up with <i>a single effect</i> that can not be duplicated by another Sphere. Even rank 1 stuff can be jerry-rigged. If you can not do this, then all Spheres are redundant and should be ignored in favor of simplicity. If you can do this once, or even twice... then congratulations you have 2, or possibly 3 spheres.<br /> <br /> <br /> You say Life 4, Mind 4, Forces 2 can &quot;bless&quot; a target. Can it ensure that is passed down genetically? Sure it can, with how many successes?<br /> <br /> Yeah you could use Forces 3, Prime 2, Matter 3, Time 4 to provide a hanging forces effect to overload a car engine... or you could just use Entropy 3. (HUGE difference in power levels there...)<br /> <br /> There is absolutely no sphere that is &quot;required&quot; if your argument is that it can be replicated somehow.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind and Entropy 5 are different things. Mind governs a shit ton of stuff, Entropy 5 is just the rank of Entropy required to affect the chaos inherent in thoughts. You can make thoughts viral, or die out naturally. Entropy 5 does NOT replicate the Mind sphere, no more than Entropy 4 replicates Life or Entropy 3 replicates Matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> You say that everything is perfectly deterministic, so is there one possible future then? If I were in your game world, and I used Mind 3/Time 3 to look into a persons memories, could I instantly determine which memory was MOST important to him? If I were to use Mind 3 / Time 3 to look into his future, could I determine exactly what needs to have him behave the way I want? If I were to use Matter 1 to scan a car, how many successes would I need to find the weakest point?<br /> <br /> <br /> The Spheres are not designed mechanically OOC to be a perfect delineation of the universe. They are designed IC to be representations of fundamental forces of the universe - which are all tangled up together, acting and interacting. By definition there MUST be some overlap. In this context, Entropy governs the fundamental force of &quot;Order&quot;. Yes, by some means of having every other sphere to near master level and amassing massive power through every cast (major successes) you could replicate almost all Entropy effects (based on the ST, of course). The mage who studies order, chaos, and the fundamental force of entropy will have a much easier time of it.<br /> <br /> I could use Correspondence to &quot;summon&quot; any force and control it through shape and relation, with enough successes. A Forces mage would have a much easier time of it.<br /> <br /> I could use Life to fuck with people's Mind, if I knew enough about the relationship between them. A Mind mage can be much more direct about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's how this game works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting points. I'm more going for mechanical delineation than representing philosophical forces for the Universe. I do accept that Spheres can overlap each other to an extent. I play Ars Magica and see that all the time. The problem I have is that, mechanically, with Entropy is it basically lets a PC mimic just about every other Sphere (probably not Spirit). By description there are almost no limits to what it cannot do at a given level - especially in terms of other Sphere's capabilities. No other Sphere can do that, and yes, some can probably mimic other spheres more than others, but Entropy is by far the worst offender. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T10:27:50-08:00","id":391618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=391101#post391101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of people focus on the &quot;decay&quot; aspect of Entropy, when the fate/fortune order/chaos stuff is more interesting and has less in common with other Spheres. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree 100%. In fact, I think the association with decay is an artifact of naming the Sphere &quot;Entropy&quot;. If it had been named something (ANYTHING) else relevant, we wouldn't see decay brought in. I think the IP is facing some of those issues. The various levels of Entropy have one focus firmly aimed at &quot;decay&quot; and those are often the aspects of that number of dots that seems redundant with the other Spheres. (E.g. Why do I need Entropy to decay or prevent decay in a material object when that seems like something that would easily come under almost all paradigmatic views of Matter? Etc. Etc. )<br /> <br /> The focus on decay is what gets Entropy uses, particularly the Euthanatos, stereotyped as necromancers, when, to most of the constituent groups in that Tradition, most of the powers people think of when they hear &quot;necromancer&quot; are downright anathema. <br /> <br /> The problem is that there is a paucity of words that accomplish encompassing the dichotomy as described by Faradn... Fate/Destiny vs. Chance/Fortune vs. Order/Chaos. And selection of one does characterize how the Sphere is percieved from then on. If you name it Change or Chaos or Luck, then you have to define order, fate, destiny as &quot;reducing the chaos in the system&quot; and vice-versa if you name it Fate/Order/Destiny. Both make the Sphere harder to work with, since fully half of it is going to be counter-intuitive. Which is another of the problems with calling it Entropy. It characterizes it so that half the uses are actually &quot;anti-Entropy&quot;. Plus that word means vastly different things to science/engineer types and everyone else. And if you pick one you really seem to be privileging technomancy or denigrating it (which isn't true, it's connecting paradigm to definition and that's not, strictly speaking, the case, or, at least, does not have to be.) <br /> <br /> I'm sure that these issues are a major reason why Awakening splits off decay into Fate (which does take out the &quot;interesting stuff&quot; that Faradn pointed out and detail it out into its own Sphere, though there are some issues with crossover/redundency with Time and Mind) and Death (which has it's own problems.... since, once again, why do I need Death to decay an object when I can use Matter? Make darkness when that seems like a lock for Forces? Make people afraid instead of using Mind? etc. ). <br /> <br /> I have toyed with a possible solution of just abolishing Prime and Entropy and having Order and Chaos, or something similar as way to deal with the situation, but it feels somehow ... off. I have never gotten past the stage of outlining it. I'm also mentally feeling out the similar idea of having Prime mean something more like &quot; Pattern&quot; and Entropy taking on &quot;Chaos&quot; with the sense of transgressing boundaries. Maybe &quot;Change&quot; would be a better name for the Sphere. All creation being a tension between the two.... Prime being the platonic ideals, the essential substance and Change/Chaos/Entropy being the lens of possibility by which those ideals are actualized in a Tapestry that isn't just iteration after iteration of idealized discrete perfections....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T10:55:57-08:00","id":391630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=391614#post391614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting points. I'm more going for mechanical delineation than representing philosophical forces for the Universe. I do accept that Spheres can overlap each other to an extent. I play Ars Magica and see that all the time. The problem I have is that, mechanically, with Entropy is it basically lets a PC mimic just about every other Sphere (probably not Spirit). By description there are almost no limits to what it cannot do at a given level - especially in terms of other Sphere's capabilities. No other Sphere can do that, and yes, some can probably mimic other spheres more than others, but Entropy is by far the worst offender.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I wouldn't say mimic, so much as affect. Entropy generally only deals with a property of patterns, not the whole pattern.<br /> <br /> And yes, Entropy is one of the two most powerful Spheres in the game, in my opinion. I agree that if you are cunning with it and your paradigm allows, it can be pretty universal. It is still limited though, in that it does not create or destroy - it perfects or decays.<br /> <br /> @Ajax<br /> <br /> Great post.<br /> <br /> Consider that while the pattern spheres are simple, and the others are easily understood... Prime is the sphere of true creation and destruction, or of &quot;what is&quot;. Entropy is the sphere of chaos and order within those things that Prime makes real, or of &quot;how is it&quot;. Entropy returns everything to Prime, and Prime takes that raw energy and creates anew.<br /> <br /> You probably could restrict the whole game to just those two spheres... but then I feel you end up missing out on a lot of the detail stuff that the other 7 provide.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also keep in mind, this stuff we are discussing right now is 100% fundamental to the paradigms of the Traditions that chair those Spheres. The two things color each other, and give them a place outside of the &quot;metagame OMG ENTROPY SO GOOD&quot; feeling you get when you really start to wrap your mind around it.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: All spheres in Ascension encompass both positive and negative aspects. Life governs Death, Entropy governs Order, Prime governs Oblivion (not the wraith type), etc. This is highlighted with Qlippothic spheres, but the potential is always there. Whatever you dictate Entropy to be called, it should govern both perfection and disorder. Prime should govern both static patterns, and dynamic flows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":2211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","user":"SixFootChicken","date":". 02-03-2015, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T14:07:14-08:00","id":391832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=391565#post391565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I added numbers to this so I can respond to them.<br /> <br /> 1.) But what is chance from purpose? Was someone a dick to me on purpose, or by accident? Mind 3 telepathy. Order from disorder? Shouldn't that be visible to the naked eye? Or even a combination of level 1 Spheres?<br /> <br /> 2.) Depends on how one wants &quot;Fate&quot; or &quot;Destiny&quot; as an independent force in your game. If you don't, (like me) then this isn't even a thing.<br /> <br /> 3.) See above.<br /> <br /> 4.) But arguably this outcomes come from a deterministic process using other spheres.<br /> <br /> 5.) Why not? And if, by description of the Sphere, what is lost by getting rid of Entropy and folding that capability into the Sphere of Mind?<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess we don't really see the Sphere in the same way then. Those seem pretty cut and dried to me and I'm not really following your train of thought. It's fine, though - I don't need to convince you or anything <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. If you think Entropy would be better folded into other Spheres, go for it. Might be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T14:41:42-08:00","id":391871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=391832#post391832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I guess we don't really see the Sphere in the same way then. Those seem pretty cut and dried to me and I'm not really following your train of thought. It's fine, though - I don't need to convince you or anything <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. If you think Entropy would be better folded into other Spheres, go for it. Might be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's become very obvious to me throughout this thread that I'm thinking of this very differently that the rest of people posting here. That's fine. My thought process is basically deterministic and game mechanics based. I'm also not liking the idea of some abstract &quot;fate&quot; that can be &quot;woven&quot;.<br /> <br /> No - to me, the limiting the Magic of the game in fact, makes it a bit more interesting. If a mage wants to do something, then they need to target that something. If they want to just so happen to find a taxi cab waiting for them when they leave a building, that needs to be a Mind 4 Corr 2 to control the mind of a taxicab driver they can't directly see or something like that vs Entropy 2* and just by &quot;random&quot; chance get the timing correct. <br /> <br /> Using Entropy 2 to &quot;randomly&quot; get the timing right avoids the fact that the PC is mind controlling a cab driver to show up at a convenient time for them. Some ST's won't let that kind of Entropy 2 effect anyway, and some will. I want to solve the argument I have in my head by just removing the whole sphere. Though really, they could just TIme 2 to find out what a cab will be near the building come out what appropriate. <br /> <br /> *Could be higher level, I'm saying 2 to pick a number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T15:00:46-08:00","id":391893,"title":"","content":"The cab thing is an interesting example. What's that acronym that views magic in this way? RBD or something? (Don't really like those acronyms, so have trouble recalling them, lol). But I can really get behind that. Correspondence 3 to &quot;teleport&quot; across town, but the mage makes it coincidental by having a cab pitch up and rides a succession of green traffic lights via little-known shortcuts. Something about that approach just really works for me - I like the way it adds a layer of the unknown to the game. So by the same token, I could get behind using Entropy 2 in a similar way. For me it hearkens back to some of the stuff in Mage 1e, where the mage doesn't always control how the magic manifests. It's a feel thing, I guess. (Also liked how players could come up with their own Paradox manifestations in 1e - but that's another tangent.)<br /> <br /> At the same time, though, I'd also support an approach like the one you talk about, using Time or Mind or Forces to actually make sure a cab arrives where and when you want it to. Lots of different cats to skin <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T15:05:54-08:00","id":391896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also not liking the idea of some abstract &quot;fate&quot; that can be &quot;woven&quot;. </div> </div> </div>This is a major part of your problem right there as Fate is a big part of Entropy Spheres influence not to mention a very important thing in many Paradigms out there, any Norse influenced Paradigm for example as well as any following old Greek roots etc.<br /> <br /> If you remove Fate as a thing in your world then it leaves Entropy a bit crippled which leads to the Sphere feeling somewhat redundant naturally. So perhaps at your table the correct thing is to remove it along with the concept of Fate. Each to his own as the saying goes.<br /> <br /> As to the official workings of it I have to agree with many if the above posters on Entropy being one of the most useful Spheres with it's strengths being Curses/Blessings, Order/Disorder, Fate, Luck/Bad Luck as well as Decay/Perfection but at the core of it it is a subtle Sphere that usually needs a bit more oomph, successes, on it to do immediate effect comparable to those of other Spheres where it excels is long term and subtle effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T15:36:45-08:00","id":391952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=391893#post391893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The cab thing is an interesting example. What's that acronym that views magic in this way? RBD or something? (Don't really like those acronyms, so have trouble recalling them, lol). But I can really get behind that. Correspondence 3 to &quot;teleport&quot; across town, but the mage makes it coincidental by having a cab pitch up and rides a succession of green traffic lights via little-known shortcuts. Something about that approach just really works for me - I like the way it adds a layer of the unknown to the game. So by the same token, I could get behind using Entropy 2 in a similar way. For me it hearkens back to some of the stuff in Mage 1e, where the mage doesn't always control how the magic manifests. It's a feel thing, I guess. (Also liked how players could come up with their own Paradox manifestations in 1e - but that's another tangent.)<br /> <br /> At the same time, though, I'd also support an approach like the one you talk about, using Time or Mind or Forces to actually make sure a cab arrives where and when you want it to. Lots of different cats to skin <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So yes, how I'm thinking is very much on the far end of the Process Based Determinism axis. If you run a game from that point of view - then Entropy seems to be stepping on other Spheres toes and actually irrelevant. However, if one is under Result Based Determinism, Entropy's purview isn't such a big deal because other Spheres are a lot more potent and indirect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">HAP/HOP/HYP and RBD/PBD are a set of complimentary theories on how magic works. They're a set of worldviews to compare and contrast that, collectively, can help you determine whether something like what you've described is coincidental or vulgar.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Under the </span></span><b>Hypothetical Average Perceiver</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> model, whether something is coincidental or vulgar is determined by whether someone standing next to you -- the &quot;average observer&quot; -- would think it's impossible or not. If you summon a business card in your pocket and then pull it out, it's coincidental, because you </span></span><i>could</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> have had a business card there.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Under the </span></span><b>Hypothetical Omniscient Perceiver</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> model, whether something is coincidental or vulgar is determined whether an omniscient observer -- someone who </span></span><i>can</i><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> see inside your pocket -- can tell whether some magic's just been done. Under this model, summoning a business card is vulgar whether you do it in your pocket or out in the open. (Doing it in your pocket is still to your advantage if you'd like to be vulgar without witnesses rather than vulgar with, however.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Under the </span></span><b>Harass Yonder Passerby</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> model, whenever something like this comes up at your gaming table, you go and find someone nearby who doesn't know what gaming is, and ask him whether it sounds like magic or not. It's a joke, but it's a well-established, traditional joke, now.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">HOP sounds really harsh until you consider the other axis.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Under </span></span><b>Result-Based Determinism</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">, magic achieves effects through circumstance, and you only need the spheres sufficient to accomplish the end result. With RBD, you can use Correspondence 3 to summon up a taxicab (a real taxicab, not one you just created) that arrives improbably fast, takes you to where you're going with trafic parting before you as the Red Sea parted before Moses, and then drives off when you get out without the driver remembering to ask you to pay. Because the spell was just &quot;Get from point A to point B,&quot; and that falls under Correspondence. The taxicab thing is the coincidence. Nobody, not even an omniscient perceiver, could tell that you used magic.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Under </span></span><b>Process-Based Determinism</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> you need magic to account for every process along the way to a spell's result. You can't summon the taxicab without Mind to control the driver, probably Entropy to make the traffic part improbably fast, and, of course, Correspondence to affect the nearest taxi before you can see it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Process-Based Determinism goes well with Hypothetical Average Perceiver. Result-Based Determinism goes well with Hypothetical Omniscient Perceiver. Mage Revised tends to go with RBD/HOP, while Mage 2nd actually tends to go with RBD/HAP. But a lot of rotes seem written by authors who subscribe to PBD.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Anyway, the answer to the question &quot;Is scrying using a PDA vulgar or coincidental?&quot; depends on the answer to the question &quot;How do you want magic to work in your game?&quot; I, personally, like RBD/HOP, because I like vulgar/coincidental to be independent of witnesses/no witnesses, but a lot of people like HAP (which I can understand), and quite a few people like PBD (which I can't).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Apparently there are some people who run HOP/PBD games. I'm not sure what sort of magic could ever count as coincidental in those</span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T20:08:23-08:00","id":392199,"title":"","content":"Well actually in my opinion the deeper you are in the PBD side of thing the more needed the Entropy Sphere is. Let's say you want to summon a Taxi at your location, in your opinion that would take Mind 4 Corr 2, according to your previous post, but with PBD all that Rote does is summon a Cab, it doesn't actually help the Cab in getting to your location it could still get stuck in traffic and leave you without a Cab when you needed one with Entropy added to the mix, governing chance and luck, could make sure that he instinctually chooses a route that avoids traffic jams and other possible problems, crash sites etc., and actually is there on time. In PBD you need Entropy to make sure some random occurrence doesn't foil your effect as those aren't covered by any other Sphere.<br /> <br /> Again YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T01:36:35-08:00","id":392437,"title":"","content":"I love how we can overcomplicate things. It must be a built in feature of being a Mage fan <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T02:37:02-08:00","id":392456,"title":"","content":"I think success levels are a factor as well. If you go with the standard idea that three successes is a complete Effect, you can achieve things with Entropy that would require more successes with other Spheres. To continue with the cab analogy, if you did it with Mind and Correspondence, you'd need to factor in Correspondence ranges and also the target's Wits threshold (without which the target will realise that something is up and may be allowed a Willpower roll to resist the Effect). So that's a bunch of extra successes on top of the basic amount required. And if you incorporate a Pattern Sphere, there's also that rule in Revised (I don't use it) that would require you to have Correspondence at the same level as other Pattern Spheres in the Effect. Entropy can do it without those extra requirements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","user":"Thebian","date":". 02-04-2015, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T16:37:58-07:00","id":1297383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/390220-is-the-sphere-of-entropy-redundant?p=391871#post391871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's become very obvious to me throughout this thread that I'm thinking of this very differently that the rest of people posting here. That's fine. My thought process is basically deterministic and game mechanics based. I'm also not liking the idea of some abstract \u201cfate\u201d that can be \u201cwoven\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with others that the notion of fate as being something that can be woven is entirely appropriate for the mystical factions of the Ascension War, I'd very much be interested in your feedback for my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/758179-fields-for-the-technocracy\">Fields for the Technocracy</a> idea. The premise is to work up an alternative to the Spheres that's more in tune with the way the Technocracy thinks. Last I checked, I had settled on: Space, Time, Void, Material, Energy, Systems, Data, Mind, and Utility. <br /> <br /> Note that these don't align precisely with the Spheres, even when you might think that they would: Material deals with flesh and bone as well as steel and stone, for example, and Data and Space are distinct Fields with very little overlap. <br /> <br /> Note also that there's no Entropy in there, nor anything directly resembling it. Entropy-like Procedures are instead handled by Data and/or Time, depending on the Procedure. <br /> <br /> Anyway, if you have any thoughts on it, feel free to reply to that thread with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-17-2019, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T07:32:21-07:00","id":1297508,"title":"","content":"I will take a look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}